  "_comment": "Codeg: two artifacts per platform, each unpacked under codeg/<directory> without the archive's top directory. The server bundle (codeg-server, codeg-mcp, codeg-computer-helper and the web UI) comes from the publisher's GitHub release, its one source, each digest from the release's .sha256 file. Node.js 22 LTS is the same nodejs.org build CloudCLI's manifest pins, pinned for every version, each digest what nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.3/SHASUMS256.txt names, and npmmirror serves the same files. The Linux server binaries need glibc 2.34, the agent's own floor.",
  "name": "codeg",
  "title": "Codeg",
  "description": "AI coding sessions in the browser from Codeg, one per account, opened from a client with a token",
